ROADMAP_VERSION 0.2.0

STATUS APPROVED

SUPERSEDES ROADMAP_VERSION 0.1.0

OWNER President Cley Duarte

ROADMAP

Ordered by execution strategy: each phase first guarantees CONTINUITY (the
product keeps working and does not forget) before pursuing GROWTH (reaching
more users and scaling). One single list; phase + continuous correlative
(FN . NN), no resets, no disorder.

PHASE_1 FOUNDATION -- the engine exists and governs itself   [DONE]
  01  Create the official PACE repository
  02  Implement the minimal skeleton
  03  Implement pace init
  04  Implement pace create
  05  Self-governance: PACE adopts itself

PHASE_2 SOLID PRODUCT -- installable, with memory and governance (continuity)
  06  Package the CLI as an installable `pace`
  07  Smoke test: install on a clean environment
  08  Define the ACTOR / ROOT_AUTHORITY in .pace/
  09  Bootstrap/Handoff engine -- the AI knows to consult the owner
  10  Guided Intake/Onboarding (pace init --guided)
  11  Per-chat memory / continuity -- no context "dementia"
  12  Test suite + CI (pytest + pace doctor)
  13  Update the README

PHASE_3 LAUNCH AND MONETIZATION -- enter the market (growth)
  14  Design the sellable structure / business model
  15  Choose and apply the license
  16  Make the landing sell (conversion)
  17  Publish the landing on GitHub Pages

PHASE_4 ADOPTION AND EXPANSION -- more users, sustained growth
  18  Upstream contribution rule with authorization
  19  User documentation: quickstart + guide
  20  Create the first new project born from PACE

PHASE_5 SCALE AND ROBUSTNESS -- grow without breaking continuity
  21  Semantic Doctor (deep validation)
  22  pace migrate (schema-version migrations)
  23  Standalone binary (PyInstaller)
  24  Stack templates for pace create

END
